re  and once again it must fight to survive  as the peaceful stability which enabled  its prosperity  is replaced with more aggressive  relations between its two  non-ally allies the cost of neutrality  will only grow in other words one day  singapore may finally be forced to  choose a side  but until that day comes it would like  for both sides to fear  the outcome singapore's natural  dependence on other countries  has led it to pursue some unusual  policies to ensure  its security for example the singaporean  government has convinced its population  to drink pea humorous as that sounds  it's absolutely not a joke to find out  what drinking pee  has to do with singapore's national  security you can watch the extended  version of this video which replaces  this ad  on our new streaming platform nebula  while these videos will continue being  available  here there are some topics and tangents  like  drinking pee that aren't quite right for  youtube but i just can't not mention  if you enjoy these videos the best way  to watch them  is before they're posted on youtube  without ads  and with specially made bonus content  from your favorite creators like  wendover productions  real engineering and rely floor on  nebula  but it gets better because we've  partnered with curiositystream where you  can watch documentaries like singapore's  field of dreams  which explains how the city built a  stadium which can adapt to hold over 30  different sports  and the rise of the gulf about the  growth of oil cities like dubai  you can get curiosity stream and nebula  for the very affordable price of just 15  bucks  a year in other words you get access to  thousands of great documentaries  you get ad-free early and bonus content  you help support creators like myself  and right now it's 26 off  it would be a crime not to take  advantage of this deal  sign up with the link in the description  and you'll get an email shortly  afterward with access to nebula


